WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.865
Medical Assistance in Dying.

00:00:02.815 --> 00:00:09.960
Since legalization in 2016, over 60,000 Canadians have died through this program.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.802
That number has grown by 1,467 percent in seven years.

00:00:15.802 --> 00:00:26.105
In 2023 alone, 15,343 Canadians received MAID — representing 4.7 percent of all deaths in the country.

00:00:26.105 --> 00:00:30.789
Canada now has the fastest-growing euthanasia program in the world.

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:35.421
The Netherlands pioneered legal euthanasia in 2002.

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:40.078
After 20 years, they reached 4.8 percent of deaths.

00:00:40.078 --> 00:00:43.684
Canada matched that rate in just 7 years.

00:00:43.684 --> 00:00:52.197
Veterans have testified to Parliament that Veterans Affairs caseworkers offered MAID during calls about wheelchair ramps and housing support.

00:00:52.197 --> 00:00:57.078
At least five separate veterans reported unsolicited MAID offers.

00:00:57.078 --> 00:01:07.565
In 2022, a 51-year-old Ontario woman with Multiple Chemical Sensitivities received MAID after years of being unable to find affordable housing.

00:01:07.565 --> 00:01:11.710
She told media: the government sees me as expendable.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:19.209
Bill C-7, passed in 2021, removed the requirement that natural death be reasonably foreseeable.

00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:23.171
It also eliminated the 10-day reflection period.

00:01:23.171 --> 00:01:27.289
MAID can now be provided the same day as the request.

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:31.131
Canada has no independent MAID oversight body.

00:01:31.131 --> 00:01:33.447
Doctors self-report.

00:01:33.447 --> 00:01:36.631
No real-time monitoring exists.

00:01:36.631 --> 00:01:40.394
The Auditor General has never audited the program.

00:01:40.394 --> 00:01:45.710
Three consecutive RCMP Commissioners — zero investigations.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:54.263
The United Nations Special Rapporteur on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities has formally raised concerns about Canada's MAID regime.

00:01:54.263 --> 00:01:59.184
The UN Human Rights Committee flagged it in their 2023 review.
